    "facts_line": "2026-11-18 (Wednesday, before the open), 27 days out -- from the earnings calendar, consensus EPS 18.84.",
    "why": "The first full quarter of the \u20ac3 EU parcel fee must show up as lower transaction-services margin; if it doesn't, the cost thesis is wrong."
  },
  "reasons": [
    "China e-commerce GMV [gross merchandise value] grew 0.9% in the June 618 festival while PDD's SG&A [selling, general and administrative costs] rose 11.4% year over year against revenue up 8.1% \u2014 spending is outrunning demand.",
    "Consensus wants EPS [earnings per share] of 18.84 on 18 November after 9.51 actual in May; two of the last three reported quarters missed by 15.8% and 41.9%.",
    "Temu has paid \u20ac3 per low-value parcel into the EU since 1 July, so the September quarter carries the fee for the first time; extra customs data from 1 November lands in Q4 guidance."
  ],
  "watch": [
    "Revenue against the 115.64B consensus: a miss confirms the short; a print above 115.64B breaks it.",
    "SG&A growth versus revenue growth: still above 8.1% confirms; below it breaks.",
    "Transaction services revenue (54.7B, +13% year over year in Q2): deceleration confirms the EU fee bite; reacceleration breaks it.",
    "Q4 guidance on the 1 November EU customs-data rule: any quantified cost confirms; 'no material impact' breaks."
  ],
